WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
Well, it is thrifty week on our show here,

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.980
and we love a theme.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.420
And winning money is fun,

4
00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:11.790
saving money is also incredibly important

5
00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.550
and very gratifying.

6
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.793
It can also be very creative.

7
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.000
We challenged our good friend,

8
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.250
celebrity designer, Mikel Welch,

9
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.450
who is a Drew Crew member

10
00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:28.219
and sustainable stylist Sarah Teresinsky.

11
00:00:28.219 --> 00:00:31.850
And they did a little upcycling challenge.

12
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:33.620
Now, upcycling is all the rage.

13
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:35.560
I think we used to call it vintage shopping,

14
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.610
and now we're calling it upcycling.

15
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.330
Because we see the value in buying older things.

16
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:42.910
Not only are they more affordable,

17
00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.270
but they can be better for our environment.

18
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:47.880
So we sent them to an incredible thrift store here

19
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.100
in New York to put their skills to the test.

20
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.630
I love this video. Take a look.

21
00:00:54.578 --> 00:00:58.060
Hey Drew, we are here outside of City Opera Thrift Shop.

22
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.780
This shop is amazing.

23
00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.580
They have been giving to the Opera community

24
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.130
here in New York city for well over 40 years.

25
00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.580
Inside, they have everything from clothes,

26
00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.200
decor, you name it.

27
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.650 line:15%
I've got my friend right here, Sarah T,

28
00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:13.088 line:15%
and she is a sustainable stylist.

29
00:01:13.088 --> 00:01:15.069
And we're gonna go head-to-head

30
00:01:15.069 --> 00:01:17.280
and pick items that we're going to upcycle.

31
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.605
That's right. Are you ready?

32
00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:20.720
Am I ready?
This is a serious challenge.

33
00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.090
Girl, I was born ready.
This is all I do.

34
00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.180
One,

35
00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.630
two,

36
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.210
two and a half, you cheated, three.

37
00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.043
No.

38
00:01:28.043 --> 00:01:29.908
(Sarah laughs)

39
00:01:29.908 --> 00:01:32.908
(adventurous music)

40
00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.910
(upbeat music)

41
00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:45.220 line:15%
(upbeat music continues)

42
00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:46.593
Think again, sister.

43
00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:49.190
That's a pretty cool lamp.

44
00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.230
I'm definitely into lamp upcycles

45
00:01:51.230 --> 00:01:52.730
'cause there's so many things you can do with these,

46
00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:53.600
especially older ones.

47
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.050
I like it but it just seems basic.

48
00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.061 line:15%
I've made all sorts of storage with books before.

49
00:01:59.061 --> 00:02:01.840 line:15%
(fun music)

50
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.330 line:15%
I love taking beautiful pieces

51
00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:06.000 line:15%
and incorporating them into an upcycle.

52
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.510
I need more fabric, but this would be a beautiful ottoman.

53
00:02:09.510 --> 00:02:11.560
Sarah, don't be over here, peeking at my stuff.

54
00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:12.560
You stay back there.

55
00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.070
Right back at you Mikel.

56
00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.290 line:15%
I need to find a jacket

57
00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.780 line:15%
that I can reupholster a ottoman with.

58
00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.610 line:15%
I mean, this has nothing to do with the challenge.

59
00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:22.443 line:15%
I'm sorry, Drew,

60
00:02:22.443 --> 00:02:23.746 line:15%
I just really want to throw this on

61
00:02:23.746 --> 00:02:25.718 line:15%
because I think it might be a good fit.

62
00:02:25.718 --> 00:02:28.620 line:15%
(fun music continues)

63
00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.660 line:15%
I'm thinking this one is a little more like masculine

64
00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:32.493 line:15%
and toned.

65
00:02:32.493 --> 00:02:34.100 line:15%
We have like straps here

66
00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.730 line:15%
or the strap fed in to here

67
00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.730 line:15%
where it's almost like a handle something.

68
00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:38.960
I found this beautiful lamp

69
00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.020
and I'm so excited to upcycle it.

70
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.329
So, I'm ready to check out, gonna head upstairs.

71
00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.530
I am ready to check out, my friend.

72
00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:46.363
All right.

73
00:02:46.363 --> 00:02:47.196
Thank you so much.

74
00:02:47.196 --> 00:02:49.051
You are so very welcome, thank you, you guys.

75
00:02:49.051 --> 00:02:51.880
(fun music)

76
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.110
So how do you feel?

77
00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.730
Oh, I feel amazing. How do you feel?

78
00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.040
I'm just telling you now, I've got it in the bag

79
00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.050
and yours needs to go in a trash bag.

80
00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.230
Mine will come out of the trash

81
00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:01.480
and look amazing when I'm done,

82
00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:02.313
'cause that's what I do.

83
00:03:02.313 --> 00:03:04.860
Well, we're gonna let Drew make the final decision.

84
00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:08.190
So Drew, we'll see you back at the studio.

85
00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:09.200
(audience cheers and applauds)

86
00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.144
I cannot wait to weigh in,

87
00:03:11.144 --> 00:03:16.144
because Mikel and Sarah are right here, live and in person.

88
00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.270
Are you guys feeling pretty confident?

89
00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.103
She's going down?

90
00:03:19.103 --> 00:03:20.780
No, no way.
She's going down.

91
00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.376
He's a big talker. He is not going down.

92
00:03:22.376 --> 00:03:23.626
I love this!
I'm going to win.

93
00:03:23.626 --> 00:03:24.500
Going down.
He's going down.

94
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.390
I'm not going down.

95
00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.520
I'm sending her back to Texas.

96
00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.800
These are the kind of fights I'm into

97
00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.840
'cause they're healthy and not scary.

98
00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.930
I'm in, and we're gonna find something creative

99
00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:34.120
and I have to tell you,

100
00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.070
we're gonna go to a quick commercial break,

101
00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.890
stick around because I wanna see

102
00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:40.160
what you guys did with the stuff.

103
00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.120
So stick around 'cause we're gonna see what you did

104
00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.066
when we come back, all right!

105
00:03:44.066 --> 00:03:45.200
And we're back

106
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.033
(audience cheers and applauds)

107
00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:49.461
with the incredibly talented designer Mikel Welch,

108
00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:50.900
and part of the Drew Crew,

109
00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.260
and his innovative challenger,

110
00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:56.190
sustainable stylist, Sarah Teresinsky.

111
00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:58.230
These pieces are incredible.

112
00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:02.630
I'm really excited to hear from each of you about process,

113
00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.150
so that we can all learn

114
00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.530
and we're gonna start with Mikel.

115
00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:09.150
Okay, so my process, honestly Drew,

116
00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.460
was pretty, pretty simple.

117
00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.210 line:15%
So the basic thing here, I had an ottoman.

118
00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.070
You can pick a old ottoman up at home,

119
00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:16.600
at a thrift store, et cetera.

120
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:19.700
I found a big oversized coat.

121
00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:21.500
Once I saw that it could cover the piece,

122
00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.310
I moved on to accessories.

123
00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.770 line:15%
I found another coat that had beautiful buttons.

124
00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.430 line:15%
And then I found a cute little leather belt,

125
00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:32.370 line:15%
cut it in half and used that as little strap handles.

126
00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.300 line:15%
But I have one other little thing I want to show you too.

127
00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:36.850
So we got the accessories done.

128
00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.730
I wanted, just like an extra element,

129
00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:39.620 line:15%
because you know how you are,

130
00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:40.970 line:15%
you want things to be practical,

131
00:04:40.970 --> 00:04:42.260 line:15%
you want them to be functional,

132
00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:44.980 line:15%
and that's like really big with whatever I bring to you.

133
00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:45.813 line:15%
It's true. You know me so well.

134
00:04:45.813 --> 00:04:49.200
So check out the front. So this was a coat.

135
00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.790
I saved the little pocket

136
00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.573
so that you can put your TV remote there.

137
00:04:55.573 --> 00:04:57.163
(adience cheers and applauds)

138
00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:58.963
(Sarah laughs)

139
00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:01.120
It's not over yet, it's not over yet.

140
00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.210
I'll tell you two reasons why I love this;

141
00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.550
I can still tell that there is coat elements.

142
00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.383
Yes.

143
00:05:08.383 --> 00:05:09.610
Because of the buttons.

144
00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:10.850
Yes absolutely.

145
00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.880
I love the leather strap.

146
00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:14.670
Certainly this tone of leather

147
00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:17.184
against the black like herringbone.

148
00:05:17.184 --> 00:05:18.210
Yes, absolutely.

149
00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.190
So there's a lot of things working for me about this.

150
00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:22.140
Glad you like it.

151
00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:23.580
All right, Sarah.

152
00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:26.900
Now, I want to see your before picture

153
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:28.900
so we can see the transition.

154
00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.810
Okay, beautiful lamps.

155
00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.330
Yeah, so a huge thing for me when I thrift

156
00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.490 line:15%
is I like to look for things that I see a lot.

157
00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:36.340 line:15%
You see a lot of lamps,

158
00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:37.450 line:15%
a lot of books, a lot of ties.

159
00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.440
So I decided to gather them together

160
00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:42.060
and create this fabulous little book situation.

161
00:05:42.060 --> 00:05:43.610
So the great thing about lamps,

162
00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.970
especially ones that are glass on the bottom

163
00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:48.980 line:15%
that are crystal, is that lamps screw apart.

164
00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:51.410 line:15%
You can screw the top, screw the bottom.

165
00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.310 line:15%
They come apart like an accordion.

166
00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.960 line:15%
And then I just took battery operated lights

167
00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:00.330
and inserted them in the bottom, up into the lantern itself.

168
00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.660
They come on and off.

169
00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:04.509
And you can use the little

170
00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:06.410
remote control, battery operated lights.

171
00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:08.350
It's so simple to slide them back up.

172
00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:09.800
You screw everything back on.

173
00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.380
I used some of the pieces that were left over.

174
00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:14.840
Obviously, I took the light bulb part, screws right off,

175
00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:15.673
and then I went through

176
00:06:15.673 --> 00:06:17.400
and I painted the bottom of this a little,

177
00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.800
took a little bit of tie.

178
00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:19.633
I see that.

179
00:06:19.633 --> 00:06:21.500
'Cause that detail was not there before.

180
00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:22.333
A little accent.

181
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:23.180
And the great thing about these

182
00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.620
is that you can use them on your table,

183
00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.440
you can hang 'em somewhere.

184
00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:28.100
And then you just take your books

185
00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:30.100
and you cover 'em, old-school with the ties,

186
00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:31.900
like we did with paper books, right?

187
00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.550
To give your books a little jazz up.

188
00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.790
And then even, I mean, you got the remote control,

189
00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:37.040
but Drew, how about

190
00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.690
when you want to hide some stuff from your kids?

191
00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:41.181
You just make a little pocket.

192
00:06:41.181 --> 00:06:42.020
(adience member exclaims)

193
00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.540
Uh-huh, You got the remote.

194
00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.706
Do I need to walk around you?

195
00:06:44.706 --> 00:06:45.539
(audience cheers and applauds)

196
00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:46.372
What?

197
00:06:47.747 --> 00:06:49.586
It is impressive.

198
00:06:49.586 --> 00:06:52.900
I love the way that you tied in the fabric.

199
00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.740
Because what I noticed about these lamps

200
00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:59.860
was how these crystal balls played into this crystal ball.

201
00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:00.710
Right.

202
00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.560
So I thought they were tied together in that element,

203
00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.660
but that was the one thing I was seeing between the two.

204
00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:11.660
The fabric really brings the glue of the whole thing.

205
00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.250
A fun little situation.

206
00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:15.980
Both pieces are really unique.

207
00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:19.040
And I think I might need a little help

208
00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.540
from the audience to pick a winner

209
00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.990
because I love you guys so much.

210
00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:23.650
I'm just not up for the challenge

211
00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:27.350
of ever dissing anything that you guys do.

212
00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:31.020
All right, everybody let's make some noise for Mikel

213
00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:32.338
if you're loving his style.

214
00:07:32.338 --> 00:07:36.483
(audience cheers and applauds)

215
00:07:36.483 --> 00:07:38.400
Mikel, it's a good one.

216
00:07:42.533 --> 00:07:43.850
Okay.

217
00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.150
Now, let's make some noise

218
00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:47.533
if you prefer Sarah's creation.

219
00:07:47.533 --> 00:07:51.723
(audience cheers and applauds)

220
00:07:51.723 --> 00:07:52.806
Well, I mean.

221
00:07:53.808 --> 00:07:56.210
(Drew laughs)

222
00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:58.800
I'm just gonna go with you both win, all right?

223
00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.020
I hereby crown you both

224
00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:06.190
The Magic Miscellaneous Material Magicians.

225
00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:11.054
And I want to thank you so much, Mikel and Sarah because

226
00:08:11.054 --> 00:08:14.607
(adience cheers and applauds)

227
00:08:14.607 --> 00:08:17.920
as much as I would love to take one of you down,

228
00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:21.630
I think that there is really merit in both approaches.

229
00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:22.770
They're very different.

230
00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:25.740
It's not an apples to apples comparison.

231
00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.370
There's something here for everyone.

232
00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:28.770
And I just love you guys

233
00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.316
and showing us and teaching us what's possible.

234
00:08:31.316 --> 00:08:32.160
Well thank you for having us.

235
00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.430
Thank you.

236
00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.610
All right, Mikel, Sarah, thank you so much.

237
00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.493
I love you both.

238
00:08:37.493 --> 00:08:40.076 line:15%
(bright music)

